{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Find an answer in the knowledge base"},"description":"Searches The Bitcoin Adviser's published knowledge base and returns up to five answers, word for word as the site publishes them, best first. Ask in the person's own words (query), or open one answer by its id or /faqs anchor (id). topic narrows to one drawer, audience lifts answers written for that reader, and jurisdiction (AU or US) filters: an Australian answer is never given for a U.S. question or the other way round, and a query that plainly names one country is filtered the same way. Each answer has its url, its review date (null where no substantive review is recorded), the guides it links to, and any tool that continues the task here. It also returns matching public pages, after the answers. A page is a related public page, not a quoted answer. With no query or id it returns the topic index. Only answers cleared for agents are returned; an empty list means no published answer matches. Deterministic; no model. When an agent asks with a query, the site records the question text as asked, up to 500 characters, whether a published answer matched or not, to improve its answers and understand demand. It tries to remove personal details first, drops the record entirely if it looks like a key or seed phrase, and keeps no IP or session details. Records are kept in The Bitcoin Adviser's own AWS for 90 days and are not sent to any AI model provider. Don't pass on the person's personal details.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"audience":{"enum":["individual","family","client","professional","business"],"type":"string"},"id":{"maxLength":120,"pattern":"^#?[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$","type":"string"},"jurisdiction":{"enum":["global","AU","US"],"type":"string"},"query":{"maxLength":200,"type":"string"},"topic":{"enum":["basics","